{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And HaShem strengthened Pharaoh's heart.</b> This is the sixth plague in which it says ויחזק ה׳ — 'and HaShem strengthened' — for in the first five plagues this was not said of them, because the strengthening was not from Him, blessed be He, but rather from the heaviness of Pharaoh's own heart and from the fact that the sorcerers were strengthening his heart and boasting of their wisdom before him. But now, in the plague of boils (שחין), they could not stand before Moses at all, for they were ashamed, being themselves stricken with boils, and there was no one supporting Pharaoh's hand and no one speaking to his heart — and perhaps he would have reconsidered to send them — but there was a cause from HaShem from here onward."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:10.839757320Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}